```toml meta
cacheable = true
l-space   = "stable"
role      = "empty a bag but keep its identity; the effect log stays"
tags      = ["lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance", "lar:///carriage.bag.clears"]
title     = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/carriage.bag.clears"
type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/carriage.bag.clears"
```

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.bag.clears ~ the residency CLEAR: a bag empties, and its identity and history log stand

`CLEAR` empties one bag and preserves its identity; the effect log keeps a deaccession for each title it took out, so the history reads whole. It takes the bag and a change-id (CLEAR carries no content to tell one change from the next, so the change-id folds into the effect key's nonce: two separate CLEARs of one bag take two ids, and the same id on a re-send reads as the same change).

A terminal asks `Proceed? [y/N]` before it submits; `--yes` names the intent off a terminal, `--dry-run` previews and commits nothing, `--in-wiki` runs the act in the active wiki's island.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ clear-a-bag · preview-first

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`clear-a-bag` params=`bag/lar:///ha.ka.ba/wikis/lares/working ~ empty the bag; its identity and its log stand`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`preview-first` params=`bag/lar:///ha.ka.ba/wikis/lares/working dry-run/true ~ name the effect and commit nothing`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ bag · change-id · dry-run · in-wiki

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`bag` params=`takes/bag-uri needs/required ~ the bag the act targets`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`change-id` params=`takes/id ~ the change's own identity, named once so a re-send reads as the same change; absent, the verb mints one`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`dry-run` params=`~ preview the effect without committing it`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`in-wiki` params=`~ run the act in the active wiki's island`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ write

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`write` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ the vessel checks the writer's cap on the destination bag; a terminal asks y/N before it submits unless --yes rides, and an agent off a terminal names --yes`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ usage · cap-denied · outcome-unknown

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[carriage.bag.clears bag/<bag>]] ~ --bag stands required`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`cap-denied` params=`~ the writer's cap on the bag falls short; nothing cleared`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`outcome-unknown` params=`~ this process stopped waiting after the vessel answered; a short read found no receipt for this attempt's request id; read it back with lares vessel request <id> before any re-run`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ done · preview · refused

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`done` params=`exit/0 fields/[[verb status requestId receipt]] ~ the vessel ran the action and wrote its effect record; the receipt names the outcome tiddler`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`preview` params=`exit/0 ~ with --dry-run the vessel names the effect it would land and commits nothing`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`refused` params=`~ the vessel refused by name (cap-denied or a verb-error); the line carries its reason and cure`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins`>>

!! skins ~ cli

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/cli`>>

!!! lares act CLEAR

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`cli` params=`spells/[[lares act CLEAR]] ~ the terminal; the verb rides as the first word, ALL-CAPS`>>
```

